UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventelevatedarchitectureonthedouble25608-20260613@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261011T161437Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260613
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261012
SUMMARY:Elevated Architecture on the Double
DESCRIPTION:ELEVATED ARCHITECTURE ON THE DOUBLE Most people walk through Downtown Frederick with absolutely no awareness of what’s happening above their own eyebrows\, which is precisely how gargoyles gain confidence. This tour aims to correct that. Many of the defining features of historic Downtown Frederick’s charming architecture are found high above the streets in upper stories\, cornices\, and spires. Maryland Double Deckers\, in partnership with Heritage Frederick\, invites you to experience Frederick’s historic buildings on the special Elevated Architecture tour. Discover beautifully preserved examples of commercial\, residential\, religious\, and public buildings displaying major American and European styles that span more than two centuries. Along the way\, we’ll explore how the history of Frederick is told by the enduring structures that witnessed it. DURATION: 1 hour 30 minutes DEPARTS FROM: Heritage Frederick\, 24 E Church St\, Frederick\, MD 21701
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/elevated-architecture-on-the-double/25608/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventfallfunfestivalatgaverfarm20763-20260904@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261011T161437Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260904
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
SUMMARY:Fall Fun Festival at Gaver Farm
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate the vibrant colors and crisp air of autumn at the Fall Fun Festival at Gaver Farm! Running throughout September and October\, this family-friendly event offers over 65 exciting attractions\, making it the perfect destination for a day of fun\, laughter\, and unforgettable memories. Explore the Corn Maze. It’s a 7-acre corn maze\, perfect for all ages. This maze combines the thrill of exploration with the joy of discovery. Whether you’re working together as a family or racing against friends\, our corn maze promises a day of fun and excitement. Meet Our Friendly Barnyard Animals: Get up close and personal with our friendly barnyard animals\, including goats\, sheep\, cow\, alpacas\, pigs\, donkey\, pony\, bunnies\, peacocks\, turkeys\, ducks and chickens. Kids (and adults!) love the opportunity to feed and interact with our goats\, creating cherished memories and learning about farm life along the way. Fall Fun Fest Admission is $20.50 per person on September weekends\, $24.00 per person on October weekends\, and $14.50 per person on weekdays. Kids under 24 months are free. Tickets are available online and in person at the farm.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/fall-fun-festival-at-gaver-farm/20763/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventfallfestivalatmagnoliameadowfarms17423-20260926@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261011T161437Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260926
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
SUMMARY:Fall Festival at Magnolia Meadow Farms
DESCRIPTION:Your Fall Starts Here! Home to Maryland’s Largest Corn Maze\, we’re more than just a pumpkin patch! Located in beautiful Northern Frederick County\, just 1 hour west of Baltimore and 1.5 hours north of D.C. Come spend a day on the farm with something for everyone to enjoy! Maryland’s Largest Corn Maze with over 5 miles of trails\, PLUS: Famous Apple Cannons Hayrides to the Pumpkin Patch Farm Animal Interactions Gem Mining Mini Ziplines Jumping Pillow Mountain Slides Pedal Karts PICK-YOUR-OWN: Sunflowers Cut flowers and wildflowers Pumpkins in all shapes\, sizes\, & colors! GATHER: Share stories around a Private Campfire! Live entertainment every Saturday & Sunday! EAT: Enjoy a farm fresh meal with local beef\, pork\, and poultry! Freshly Made Apple Cider Donuts Freshly Made Kettle Corn Beer & Wine (21+\, ID required) SHOP: Pick up locally made products! Farm Fresh Honey Goat Milk Soap Baked Goods Magnolia Meadow Farms t-shirts\, sweatshirts\, & hats HOURS: September 26 - November 1 Saturdays: 10:00am to 8:00pm Sundays: 10:00am to 6:00pm Check our website for special days & hours!
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/fall-festival-at-magnolia-meadow-farms/17423/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventmakingpizzafromscratch26029-20260926@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261011T161437Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260926
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261012
SUMMARY:Making Pizza from Scratch
DESCRIPTION:In this 2.5-hour hands-on class\, you will learn how to make pizza from scratch\, pull some fresh mozzarella\, and select from many ingredients to top your pizza including fresh veg and herbs growing seasonally at Chocolates and Tomatoes Farm. We use propane-powered portable outdoor pizza ovens. NOTE: OUTDOORS CLASS Chef Mark will do the following and then participants will practice on their own and go home with their own personal-sized pizza. Demonstrate how to make the pizza dough Show how to shape the dough for your pizza Demonstrate how to make fresh mozzarella cheese Provide tips on selecting the fresh veggie and herb options for your pizza (and talk about how we grow them on the farm) Show how to cook the pizza in the oven Operate the oven when you are cooking your pizza No cooking experience necessary. We will have hot coffee and tea\, and cold water available\, Feel free to bring nonalcoholic beverages with you. Classes are designed for adults. Teens and tweens may attend with a supportive\, registered adult. S ign up for future classes and see what else is going on at the farm here: https://www.chocolatesandtomatoes.com/ Chef Mark enjoys sharing what he has learned in his 35+ year cooking career and through his pastry arts training at La'Academie de Cuisine. Although we just launched The Learning Kitchen at Chocolates and Tomatoes Farm in 2023\, Chef Mark has been mentoring others throughout his career and teaching culinary arts at Frederick Community College since 2019.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/making-pizza-from-scratch/26029/
END:VEVENT
