UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventfrederickski26boardswapsale21621-20261010@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261011T161437Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261010
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261012
SUMMARY:Frederick Ski & Board Swap/Sale
DESCRIPTION:Maryland's Premier Ski & Snowboard Consignment Sale is Back! Winter is coming! Whether you're shopping for your first day on the slopes or replacing your entire setup\, you'll find incredible bargains at the Frederick Ski Swap. Shop the Region's Largest Ski & Snowboard Consignment Sale. Browse thousands of new\, gently used\, and lease-return skis\, snowboards\, apparel\, and accessories from outdoor retailers and individual consignors throughout Maryland\, Pennsylvania\, and Washington\, D.C. What You'll Find: Equipment • Skis • Snowboards • Boots • Bindings • Poles Apparel • Ski Jackets • Snow Pants • Base Layers • Gloves • Snow Boots Accessories • Helmets • Goggles • Bags & Packs • And much more! Top Brands: The North Face • Patagonia • Burton • Oakley • Helly Hansen • Spyder • Obermeyer • Marmot • 686 • Under Armour • UGG • Sorel and many more! Sizes Available: Toddler 4T through Adult 2XL. Wear leggings or shorts under your clothes and bring socks so you can easily try on boots and outerwear before you buy. Payment Options: We accept: • Cash • Visa • MasterCard • Venmo A 3% processing fee applies to credit card and Venmo purchases. Please note\, for everyone's safety and convenience: • No food or drinks inside the shopping area. • No personal ski or snowboard equipment may be brought into the building while shopping.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/frederick-ski-%26-board-swap-sale/21621/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventwildharvestweekend3amushroom26medicineforagingretreat25998-20261010@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261011T161437Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261010
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261012
SUMMARY:Wild Harvest Weekend: Mushroom & Medicine Foraging Retreat
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a weekend immersed in the abundance of the autumn! This hands-on foraging retreat invites you to slow down\, reconnect with the natural world\, and deepen your relationship with the plants and fungi that surround us. Together\, we will explore the forest through mindful observation\, mushroom hunting\, herbal traditions\, and shared meals. Throughout the weekend\, you’ll gain practical skills for safely identifying\, harvesting\, and working with seasonal forest gifts while enjoying time for rest\, reflection\, and community. Retreat Schedule Friday Evening (Optional Early Arrival | $65 per room Additional Cost) Arrive early and settle into the peaceful rhythm of the land. Enjoy extra time to explore\, rest\, and connect before the retreat begins. Saturday\, October 10 9:30 AM | Nature Sit Spot & Journaling with Lydia Hadfield Begin the day with a quiet sit spot practice\, guided reflection\, and journaling to deepen your awareness of the seasonal landscape. 11:00 AM Boxed lunch from Nourish Nest & head to field trip location 12:00 PM | Mushroom Foray Field Trip with Samantha Feld Learn to identify common edible mushroom species found in Maryland during the autumn months while building confidence in safe\, ethical harvesting. We’ll begin with an introduction to mushroom ecology and identification techniques\, then head into the woods to practice finding mushrooms in their natural habitat. After our foray\, we’ll review our discoveries\, discuss how to verify identifications using field guides and other resources\, and\, if we’re fortunate enough to find edible species\, cook and enjoy them together. Please come prepared to walk off-trail and explore the forest. Good woods shoes or boots and a water bottle are required. Optional tools include a collecting basket or cardboard box\, camera and/or notebook\, tick protection\, and paper lunch bags for separating finds. 4:00 PM | Rest & Reflection Time Enjoy quiet time to relax\, explore the farm\, or reflect on the day’s discoveries. 5:00 PM | Community Dinner with Nourish Nest Gather together for a shared meal featuring seasonal flavors. Dinner will be either a community-cooked meal or a catered dinner (details to be announced). 8:00 PM | Fireside Storytelling with Lydia Hadfield End the evening around the fire with stories\, conversation\, and connection. Sunday Restful Morning & Breakfast Buffet Savor your meal\, sip a warm cup of tea or coffee\, and take time to rest\, explore the farm\, journal\, or simply soak in the peaceful beauty of the morning before we gather for our final workshop. 10:00 AM Optional Movement Practice with Alecks Moss Begin the day with an optional guided movement practice to gently awaken your body\, quiet your mind\, and prepare for a day of exploration in nature. 11:00 AM Optional Sauna Time 1:00 PM | Foraging & Crafting Syrup from Wild Cherry Bark with Holly Poole-Kavana Tree bark holds some of the forest’s most concentrated plant compounds and has long been used in traditional herbal practices. In this hands-on class\, we’ll explore wild cherry bark\, learning how to identify and responsibly harvest from cherry trees while creating a simple herbal preparation to take home. 3:30 PM | Closing Circle & Depart Overnight stay & Meals included. Rooms will be selected on a first-come\, first-served basis in Fox House. All rooms are shared. (View lodging: https://foxhavenfarm.org/rentals-retreats/) Optional Friday Early Arrival Available ($65 per room)
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/wild-harvest-weekend%3a-mushroom-%26-medicine-foraging-retreat/25998/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventforagingandcraftingsyrupfrombarkwithhollypoolekavana25999-20261011@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261011T161437Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261011
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261012
SUMMARY:Foraging and Crafting Syrup from Bark with Holly Poole-Kavana
DESCRIPTION:Tree bark holds some of the most concentrated flavor and plant compounds in the forest. With the right approach\, wild cherry bark can be transformed into a simple\, effective cough syrup with both flavor and traditional use. In this hands-on class\, we’ll learn how to identify and responsibly gather bark from a wild cherry tree\, focusing on safe harvesting and field recognition. Together\, we’ll work with bark to observe how heat and time shape what is drawn from the plant and how those qualities express themselves in the finished syrup. We’ll close by discussing how bark-based preparations fit into broader herbal practice and how to continue working with them in a simple\, informed way. Meet Your Teacher Holly Poole-Kavana is a botanist and herbalist practicing in Washington\, DC. She is a lifelong plant enthusiast and has a bachelor’s degree in botany. In 2005 she shifted her focus to herbal medicine and studied with a series of experienced herbalists in the classroom\, clinic\, and outdoors. Since 2010 she has operates Little Red Bird Botanicals\, a small business that provides individual herbal consultations\, an herbal CSA (Community Supported Agriculture)\, locally-grown herbal products\, and education. Holly also works as a birth assistant and labor doula.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/foraging-and-crafting-syrup-from-bark-with-holly-poole-kavana/25999/
END:VEVENT
